 "plaques": [
  {
   "at": [
    20.2,
    0,
    -3.3
   ],
   "rot": -35,
   "text": "THE LAST SHORE\n\nHere the road out of the kingdom runs out of world.\n\nPilgrims came this far carrying one flame apiece. The wise gave theirs to the watchfires. The rest are still out in the shallows, holding them."
  },
  {
   "at": [
    -19.0,
    2.4,
    3.4
   ],
   "rot": 115,
   "text": "THE FIRST LIGHT\n\nBefore the basilica, before the bells, there was one lantern on one rock, and a man who swore to keep it.\n\nEverything the kingdom remembers began as his shift. He was the first of thirteen sworn to it \u2014 wake, watch, wait \u2014 and nobody ever relieved him. They say the last of them stands his watch still, up the hill, in armour that is not his own."
  }
 ],
